%[text] ## Try Curvilinear Regression on Your Own
%[text] - Learn to import datasets, generate and visualize polynomial data, fit polynomial regression models, and use those models to predict and visualize future values. Apply these techniques to real-world examples involving centrifugal pump performance and bioreactor systems in [Practice Curvilinear Regression: Polynomial Functions](file:../../Scripts/TryCurvilinearPolynomial.m). \
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Illustration of a rechargeable battery](text:image:6b85)
%[text] - Learn to import datasets and transform linearizable nonlinear relationships into linear regression models. Build curvilinear regression models for battery lifetime and motor heat rise with thermal saturation, then use those models to predict future values in [Practice Curvilinear Regression: Linearizable Functions](file:../../Scripts/TryCurvilinear.m). \
%%
%[text] ## **Summary** 
%[text] **Curvilinear regression** is used when the relationship between variables is not well captured by a straight line. We consider it when visual patterns in the data suggest curvature, when residuals from a linear model show systematic deviations, when domain knowledge implies nonlinearity, or when statistical metrics indicate improved model fit. Unlike linear regression, which assumes a constant rate of change, **curvilinear regression** allows us to model more nuanced relationships such as diminishing returns, tipping points, or saturation effects that are common in real-world scenarios. By fitting polynomial or nonlinear models, **curvilinear regression** provides a more accurate and meaningful representation of complex dynamics.
%%
%[text] ## Glossary
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_6fe4] **Curvilinear regression:** A method for modeling curved relationships between variables, often using polynomial or nonlinear functions. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:H_C843FC97)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_8b37] **Linearizable nonlinear regression**: A method for modeling relationships between variables using equations that are not linear in their parameters. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_0916)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_6813] **Polynomial regression**: A type of regression that models data using a polynomial equation, useful for capturing curved trends. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_4740)
%%
%[text] ## References
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_2ace] [Thiam, H. I., Owusu, V., Schuler, J., Lambarraa-Lehnhardt, F., & Hathie, I. (2025). Impact of soil salinity adaptation on yields and food security in Fimela, Senegal. Climatic Change.](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10584-025-03979-4)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_857a] [Biology Insights. (2025, April 29). Soil Salinization: Impacts and Innovative Solutions. https://biologyinsights.com/soil-salinization-impacts-and-innovative-solutions/](https://biologyinsights.com/soil-salinization-impacts-and-innovative-solutions)
